## Cursor agent instructions

<!-- V2: deep per-agent optimisation is deferred to HU-047 §10 Fase 2; this is the valid V1 minimum. -->

Cursor pre-compiles the FlowForge agents into `.md` files under `ide/cursor/agents/`.

- **Agents are pre-compiled**: inside a Cursor agent context you do NOT load `SKILL.md` files
  manually — the methodology is already embedded. Load a skill by path only when told to.
- **Rules live in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`.** When `workflow.mdc` is active it overrides this file for
  runtime behaviour; `AGENTS.md` remains the skill index and the checkpoint contract.
- Keep the legacy `.cursorrules` and `.cursor/rules/` consistent with each other and with
  `AGENTS.md` — do not let one drift.
- The checkpoint table (CKP-0 through CKP-4) is authoritative in both places; never silently skip a
  red checkpoint.
